values ('catalogue', 'wikidata', 'Q12418', 'Mona Lisa', 'Leonardo da Vinci', '{"nationality":"Italian","lifeDates":"1452–1519"}'::jsonb,
  'c. 1503–19', 'Oil on poplar panel', '79.4 × 53.4 cm', 53.4, 79.4,
  'Musée du Louvre, Paris', 'Probably a portrait of Lisa Gherardini, wife of the Florentine merchant Francesco del Giocondo. Leonardo worked on it for years and never handed it over, taking it with him to France. Soft transitions of light and shade (sfumato) give the face and the hazy landscape behind it their famous ambiguity. Its theft from the Louvre in 1911 helped make it the most famous painting in the world.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/mona-lisa.jpg',
  1074, 1600, true, 'Image: Wikimedia Commons (C2RMF), public domain', 'https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q12418')
