  '1624', 'Oil on canvas', '83 × 67.3 cm', 67.3, 83,
  'The Wallace Collection, London', 'The title is a 19th-century invention: the sitter, 26 years old according to the inscription, is smiling rather than laughing. Hals shows off his quick, confident brushwork in the lace collar and the embroidered sleeve. The painting caused a bidding war in Paris in 1865 when it was bought by the 4th Marquess of Hertford, whose collection became the Wallace Collection.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/laughing-cavalier.jpg',
