values ('catalogue', 'wikidata', 'Q185372', 'Girl with a Pearl Earring', 'Johannes Vermeer', '{"nationality":"Dutch","lifeDates":"1632–1675"}'::jsonb,
  'c. 1665', 'Oil on canvas', '44.5 × 39 cm', 39, 44.5,
  'Mauritshuis, The Hague', 'Not a commissioned portrait but a tronie: a Dutch study of a face, here a girl in an exotic turban turning to look over her shoulder. Nobody knows who modelled for it. Against a dark background, Vermeer builds her face out of soft light, with a single bright highlight on the large pearl.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/girl-pearl-earring.jpg',
