values ('catalogue', 'met', '12127', 'Madame X (Madame Pierre Gautreau)', 'John Singer Sargent', '{"nationality":"American","lifeDates":"1856–1925"}'::jsonb,
  '1883–84', 'Oil on canvas', '208.6 × 109.9 cm', 109.9, 208.6,
  'The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York', 'Sargent painted Virginie Amélie Avegno Gautreau, an American-born Parisian society beauty, in a black satin gown that sets off her powdered skin. Shown at the Paris Salon of 1884, it caused a scandal, partly because one jewelled strap had slipped from her shoulder; Sargent later repainted it in place. He kept the picture for over thirty years before selling it to the Met in 1916.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/madame-x.jpg',
  840, 1600, true, 'Image: The Metropolitan Museum of Art, CC0', 'https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/12127')
