values ('catalogue', 'met', '436532', 'Self-Portrait with a Straw Hat', 'Vincent van Gogh', '{"nationality":"Dutch","lifeDates":"1853–1890"}'::jsonb,
  '1887', 'Oil on canvas', '40.6 × 31.8 cm', 31.8, 40.6,
  'The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York', 'Painted in Paris, where Van Gogh made dozens of self-portraits because he couldn''t afford to pay models. The short, separate strokes of colour show what he was learning from the Impressionists and Neo-Impressionists. To save money he painted it on the back of an earlier canvas, The Potato Peeler, from his dark Dutch period.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/van-gogh-straw-hat.jpg',
