  'The National Gallery, London', 'A horse-drawn hay cart crosses the River Stour near Flatford Mill in Suffolk, the countryside Constable grew up in. The cottage on the left belonged to a local farmer, Willy Lott. Little noticed when first shown in London, the painting won a gold medal at the Paris Salon of 1824.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/hay-wain.jpg',
