  '1906', 'Oil on canvas', '89.9 × 94.1 cm', 94.1, 89.9,
  'The Art Institute of Chicago', 'From the late 1890s Monet painted the water garden at his home in Giverny again and again, eventually making around 250 pictures of it. Here there is no horizon and no bank, only the surface of the pond, so lily pads floating on the water mix with reflections of the sky and trees.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/water-lilies.jpg',
