  '1839', 'Oil on canvas', '90.7 × 121.6 cm', 121.6, 90.7,
  'The National Gallery, London', 'The warship Temeraire, which fought at the Battle of Trafalgar in 1805, is towed up the Thames by a small steam tug to be broken up. Turner sets the pale old sailing ship against a blazing sunset, a farewell to the age of sail. He called it his ''darling'' and would not sell it.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/fighting-temeraire.jpg',
