  '1889', 'Oil on canvas', '73.7 × 92.1 cm', 92.1, 73.7,
  'The Museum of Modern Art, New York', 'Painted in June 1889 at the asylum in Saint-Rémy-de-Provence, where Van Gogh had admitted himself. The view is based on what he saw from his east-facing window before sunrise, but the village and its church spire came from his imagination. The flame-like cypress joins the earth to a sky full of swirling movement.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/starry-night.jpg',
