  'c. 1830–32', 'Woodblock print; ink and colour on paper', '25.7 × 37.9 cm', 37.9, 25.7,
  'The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York', 'From the series Thirty-six Views of Mount Fuji. A huge wave curls over three boats of rowers while Mount Fuji sits small and still in the distance. As a woodblock print it was made in large numbers and sold cheaply; this is one of many surviving impressions. The design later fascinated European artists.', 'Written for Salon', '/art/starter/great-wave.jpg',
